nio: trace the exec_mach_imgact path to find where launchd stalls

694 froze right after "exec create_task_and_map_image" (kern_exec.c's
exec_mach_imgact enter) with no further output: exec_mach_imgact is the
last marked step and has no probes inside it.  Add a full set of marks in
one round (no drip-feeding): around load_machfile(), and inside it around
pmap_create / vm_map_create / parse_machfile.  Whichever mark is last on
the panel names the exact stall.  Uses the existing direct-console mark
mechanism so the lines survive the console being busy.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
index ed7a19b..d169da3 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -1340,9 +1340,11 @@ grade:
 	/*
 	 * Actually load the image file we previously decided to load.
 	 */
+	nio_emark("\nnio: EX: before load_machfile");
 	boot_progress_process_stage(proc_getpid(p),p->p_name,"exec load_machfile enter");
 	lret = load_machfile(imgp, mach_header, thread, &map, &load_result);
 	boot_progress_process_stage(proc_getpid(p),p->p_name,"exec load_machfile returned");
+	nio_emark("\nnio: EX: after load_machfile");
 	if (lret != LOAD_SUCCESS) {
 		error = load_return_to_errno(lret);
 
